* {{audio|fr|Fr-n'y a-t-il.oga|audio}}

===Verb===
{{head|fr|verb form|head=[[n']][[y]] [[a]][[-t-]][[il]]}}

# {{form of|fr|negative form|y a-t-il}}; isn't there? aren't there?
#: {{uxi|fr|'''N'y a-t-il''' rien à faire ?|'''Isn't there''' anything to do?}}
#: {{uxi|fr|'''N'y a-t-il''' pas de trains ?|'''Aren't there''' any trains?}}

====Usage notes====
* This fragment is typically used either with a negative adverb, such as {{m|fr|pas}} or {{m|fr|jamais}}, or with a negative object, such as {{m|fr|rien}}. Hence "N'y a-t-il ''pas'' de trains ?", "N'y a-t-il ''rien'' à faire ?", and so on. See ''{{l|fr|ne}}''.